From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:33:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] inkobj: Load, save, scale and box ink as Windows 11 does.

Measured on build 29671: a stream that is not ink serialized format at all
(another version, a size past its end) is E_UNEXPECTED; an empty array loads
as nothing; the data is looked at before whether the ink has strokes; a
format Save does not know is saved as ISF, while GIF of no strokes is
E_UNEXPECTED; an array of strings is no extended property; and a stroke's
button bits are not in its packets.  Scaled to a rectangle, a stroke keeps
its pen and its points fill the rectangle taken in by half the pen's width,
halves rounding to even.  Where Windows takes less than Wine -- a packet
description in CreateStroke, points of a stroke without X or Y, two
hand-made samples -- the test says so with todo_wine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/inkobj/attributes.c b/dlls/inkobj/attributes.c
index 39fc089fcd6..9e408b890e5 100644
--- a/dlls/inkobj/attributes.c
+++ b/dlls/inkobj/attributes.c
@@ -345,6 +345,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI extended_properties_Add(IInkExtendedProperties *iface, BST
     if (out) *out = NULL;
     if (!guid_str || FAILED(IIDFromString(guid_str, &guid)))
         return E_INVALIDARG;
+    /* ISF has no way to keep an array of strings, and Windows 11 refuses one */
+    if (V_VT(&data) == (VT_ARRAY | VT_BSTR))
+        return E_INVALIDARG;
     return extended_properties_set(properties, &guid, &data, out);
 }
 
